After installing express-session (npm install express-session), setting up session middleware:

import session from 'express-session';

app.use(session({
  secret: process.env.SESSION_SECRET, // signs the session ID cookie itself
  resave: false,
  saveUninitialized: false,
  cookie: { maxAge: 60 * 60 * 1000, httpOnly: true } // 1 hour, JS cannot access this cookie
}));

Creating a session at login (directly replacing lesson 4's jwt.sign call):

app.post('/login', async (req, res, next) => {
  // ... credential verification from lesson 3, identical either way ...
  req.session.userId = user._id.toString(); // express-session handles
                                              // generating the ID, storing
                                              // this data, and setting the
                                              // Set-Cookie header automatically
  res.json({ success: true, data: { email: user.email } });
});

Checking a session on a later, protected request:

if (!req.session.userId) {
  return res.status(401).json({ success: false, error: 'Authentication required' });
}
// req.session.userId is automatically available, having been looked up
// from the cookie's session ID by express-session's middleware already

