After installing express-rate-limit (npm install express-rate-limit):

import rateLimit from 'express-rate-limit';

const loginLimiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, // 15 minute window
  max: 5, // limit each IP to 5 login attempts per window
  message: { success: false, error: 'Too many login attempts, please try again later' },
  standardHeaders: true
});

app.post('/login', loginLimiter, async (req, res, next) => {
  // ... the same credential-verification logic from lessons 3-5 ...
});

This is applied as middleware (Module 7, lesson 8's composition pattern, now applied to a third distinct concern alongside authentication and authorization from lesson 6), running before the actual login logic, and automatically responding with a 429 'Too Many Requests' status once a given source exceeds the configured limit within the time window, without the route handler itself needing any awareness of this check at all.

